From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:16:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server, ntdll: Impersonate the client of a named pipe, as its
 quality of service asks.

ImpersonateNamedPipeClient() gave the server its own process token.  The client's security quality
of service now goes with the open request, and the server end keeps the client's security context:
a copy taken when the client connects when it is tracked statically, and for dynamic tracking the
token of the client thread as it is when it writes what the server reads.  Impersonating copies that
at the level the client allows, without the privileges it has disabled when only its effective
ones count; a client that asks for nothing is tracked dynamically with its effective privileges.
Before a client connects, and once the server has disconnected it, there is nothing to impersonate.

The Click-to-Run service impersonates Office at every lookup of its virtual registry; Word, Excel
and PowerPoint start and save as before.  The seven impersonation todos of kernel32's pipe test pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

